<title>ITALY: Italy's Genoa sees Jan CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Genoa sees Jan CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>GENOA, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Genoa said its January consumer price index stood at 0.3 percent month-on-month and 1.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In December, Genoa's inflation rate was 0.0 percent and 1.6 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Genoa is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.88 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index			0.3  (0.0)     1.8  (1.6)</p>
<p>    Food				   0.2  (0.0)     2.0  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	    0.0  (0.2)     2.9  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges    0.9  (0.1)     4.2  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			    0.0 (-0.1)     0.9  (0.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		    2.3  (0.0)     2.8  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    -0.7  (0.2)     1.7  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture	0.9 (-0.3)     0.4 (-0.4)</p>
<p>    Education			    0.0  (0.0)     4.5  (3.9)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	   0.2  (0.0)     1.8  (1.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 -0.7 (-0.1)    -2.2 (-1.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
